`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The POM's declared `<dependencies>` only capture compile-scope types a class's *field/method signatures* need to load. A class can still reference a type from an undeclared artifact in its method bodies (here, `OtlpGrpcLogRecordExporterBuilderCustomizer` implementing a `ConfigurationPropertiesCustomizer<OtlpGrpcLogRecordExporterBuilder>` from the exporter artifact) — Spring Boot guards activation with `@ConditionalOnClass`, so the autoconfiguration simply no-ops if that jar is absent, silently producing zero coverage instead of a build failure. That's why POM inspection alone wasn't enough; I had to decompile the sources and cross-reference the only prior sibling that depends on this exact artifact.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

Decision:

